From 4877ffd7ce13a8786da58c00bad5ce8cf1660b10 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: teleop-bench <325283884+teleop-bench@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 23:18:25 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 12/16] M0 6.1 instrument rev 6: pending-sample latch (fix
 peripheral under-sampling)

Smoke-2 (TIFSDIAG calls=2 role=1) CONFIRMED the role-path/hook-placement cause: the
peripheral's normal one-pair response TX completes via isr_done, not isr_tx, so the
previous-ISR tifs_prog_prev scheme captured only the exceptional continued exchanges.

Rev 6 replaces it with a PENDING-SAMPLE LATCH (reviewed design):
- LATCH the programmed tifs/phy WHEN the RX->TX switch is configured -- peripheral
  prepare for the FIRST switch (lll_peripheral.c) + isr_tx for continuing switches --
  via the exported bt_ctlr_tifs_latch(). The sample is LABELLED with this latched tifs,
  never the current lll->tifs_tx_us (which may have moved across the FSU transition ->
  wrong-plateau assignment).
- ARM exactly one pending sample on a CRC-good RX (tifs_on_rx_crc_ok); never on CRC
  fail / abort / no-RX.
- CONSUME it once at whichever completion route runs: isr_tx (continuing) OR, NEW, at
  the very start of isr_done (final one-pair response) BEFORE lll_isr_status_reset().
  Consume clears the arm; a second visit is counted as stale/duplicate, never
  re-consumed. Validity is never inferred merely from entering isr_done.
- Retires tifs_prog_prev + the first-post-clear prime skip (the latch is always
  accurate). TIFSDIAG now reports prog/arm/cons_tx/cons_done/stale_done/dup/drop.

Peripheral rebuilds clean; central unaffected (bench off there). Hardware validation
is smoke-3.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
